#: passwords.cpp:40
msgid "Echo Characters As"
msgstr "Ego Karakters As"

#: passwords.cpp:42
msgid ""
"You can select the type of visual feedback given when you enter a password "
"in kdesu. Choose one of the following options:"
"<p> "
"<ul>"
"<li><em>1 star:</em> each character you type is shown as an asterisk (*) "
"symbol.</li> "
"<li><em>3 stars:</em> three asterisks are shown for each character you "
"type.</li> "
"<li><em>no echo:</em>"
" there is no visual feedback at all, so nothing on your screen shows how "
"many characters are in your password.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""
"Jy kan kies die tipe van visuele terugvoer gegewe wanneer Jy invoer 'n "
"wagwoord in kdesu. Kies een van die volgende opsies:"
"<p> "
"<ul>"
"<li><em>1 ster:</em> elke karakter Jy tipe is vertoon as 'n asterisk (*) "
"simbool.</li> "
"<li><em>3 sterre:</em> drie sterretjie word vertoon vir elke karakter Jy "
"tipe.</li> "
"<li><em>nee ego:</em> daar is nee visuele terugvoer na alle, sodat niks op "
"jou skerm vertoon hoe veel karakters word in jou wagwoord.</li></ul>"

#: passwords.cpp:49
msgid "&1 star"
msgstr "1 ster"

#: passwords.cpp:50
msgid "&3 stars"
msgstr "3 sterre"

#: passwords.cpp:51
msgid "&No echo"
msgstr "Nee ego"

#: passwords.cpp:56
msgid "&Remember passwords"
msgstr "Onthou wagwoorde"

#: passwords.cpp:57
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, kdesu will remember your passwords for the "
"specified amount of time. Until then, you won't have to enter your password "
"again. Keep in mind that this option is insecure and may enable others to "
"damage your system."
"<p> Please <em>do not</em>"
" use this option if you are working in an insecure environment, for example, "
"on a workstation that is located in a publicly accessible area."
"<p> This option does not affect passwords explicitly set in other "
"applications, for example, your email account password in KMail."
msgstr ""

#: passwords.cpp:70
msgid ""
"You can specify how long kdesu will remember your passwords. A short timeout "
"is more secure than a long timeout."
msgstr ""
"Jy kan spesifiseer hoe lang kdesu sal onthou jou wagwoorde. 'n kort "
"tydverstreke is meer beveilig as 'n lang tydverstreke."

#: passwords.cpp:73
msgid "&Timeout:"
msgstr "Tydverstreke:"

#: passwords.cpp:76
msgid " min"
msgstr " min"

#: passwords.cpp:189
msgid ""
"<h1>Passwords</h1> This module gives you options for configuring the way in "
"which the \"kdesu\" program treats passwords. Kdesu will ask you for a "
"password when you try to carry out some privileged actions, such as changing "
"the date/time stored in your system clock, or adding new users on your "
"computer."
"<p> You can configure the type of visual feedback given when you type a "
"password, and whether kdesu should remember passwords for some time after "
"you have given them."
"<p> Note that these settings affect <em>only</em>"
" kdesu. This means that the behavior of passwords in KMail and other "
"programs cannot be configured here."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Wagwoorde</h1> Hierdie module gee jy opsies vir konfigurering van die "
"weg in wat die \"kdesu\" program handteer Wagwoorde. kdesu sal vra jy vir 'n "
"wagwoord wanneer jy probeer na voer uit sommige bevoorregde aksies, soos as "
"verandering die datum/tyd gestoor in jou stelsel horlosie, van bygesit nuwe "
"gebruikers op jou rekenaar."
"<p>"
" jy kan konfigureer die tipe van visuele terugvoer gegewe wanneer jy tipe 'n "
"wagwoord, en hetsy kdesu moet onthou Wagwoorde vir sommige tyd na jy het "
"gegewe hulle."
"<p> Nota wat hierdie instellings affekteer <em>slegs</em> kdesu. Hierdie "
"beteken wat die gedrag van Wagwoorde in Kpos en ander programme kan nie wees "
"gekonfigureer hier."

